# Generated outputs, not sources.
#
# `githubmirror/` is written by the pipeline (each run rewrites the config
# lists) and `qr-codes/` is produced alongside them from those lists. No human
# edits either directory — the published layout is described in
# docs/user/config-files.md, and the update job commits them on a schedule.
#
# `linguist-generated` is what GitHub reads to treat a path as generated: the
# file is collapsed in diff views and marked as generated in the file listing.
# `qr-codes/` holds PNG, so it also carries the `binary` macro (`-diff -merge
# -text`) rather than relying on content detection.
#
# Deliberately NOT matched: everything hand-written — `source/`, `docs/`,
# `.github/`, the root text files, and the config lists a human maintains under
# `source/config/` (`URLS.txt`, `servers.txt`, the whitelists). Those are
# sources and must keep appearing as one in diffs.
githubmirror/** linguist-generated=true
qr-codes/** linguist-generated=true binary
